# The Azure VM's own settings, appended to its .env by provision.sh. Each is measured, not
# chosen: 2026-09-28, on D8ads_v5 (8 vCPU AMD EPYC, 32 GB) and F16s_v2 (16 vCPU Intel), against
# the laptop (i9-11900H + RTX 3050 Ti). Numbers and method: studio/deploy/README.md.

# No GPU encoder here: the browser's "prefer-hardware" is refused and the render would fall back
# to the ffmpeg pipe (13.5 fps, x264 VMAF 95.5, 6.5 GB). The browser's own software H.264 draws
# and encodes in the page: 35 fps at 6 browsers, VMAF 99.99 (line art) / 99.1 (painted) at 12M.
STUDIO_RENDER_ENCODE=browser
VIDEDIT_WEBCODECS=software
# 5M scored 91.6 on a painted film, 8M 97.4, 12M 99.1 -- and 12 Mbps is YouTube's own upload
# recommendation for 1080p60, which is where a published master goes
VIDEDIT_WEBCODECS_BITRATE=12M
# 4 browsers 31.6 fps, 6 35.0, 8 33.7: past the cores it only costs memory (4.0 GB at 6)
STUDIO_RENDER_JOBS=6
STUDIO_BROWSERS=6
# the web copy on libx264: veryfast (p2) 16 s per 48 s of film, medium 39 s, same VMAF 99.99
STUDIO_WEB_PRESET=p2
# the laptop's timeouts, scaled: the render is ~1.5x slower here, the web copy is new CPU work;
# Whisper (46 s vs 2.5-4 min) and the soundtrack master (35 s vs 66 s) are faster
STUDIO_MACHINE_SLOWDOWN=2
# a film asked for from the VM itself runs on the Claude subscription, as on the laptop: Claude Code
# is installed natively (~/.local/bin/claude) and signed in by a CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN from
# `claude setup-token`, kept only in the VM's .env (deploy/README.md). Without one, set
# STUDIO_LOCAL_AUTH=api here.
